===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*werh₁-}}
From {{der|en|fro|verbal}}, from {{der|en|LL.|verbālis|t=belonging to a [[word]]}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|en|verb|al}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈvɜː.bəl/|[ˈvɜː.bɫ̩]}}, {{enPR|vûrʹ-bəl}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈvɝ.bəl/|[ˈvɜ˞.bɫ̩]}}, {{enPR|vûrʹ-bəl}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-verbal.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-verbal.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ver|bal}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)bəl|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of or relating to [[word]]s.
#: {{syn|en|wordish}}
# Concerned with the words, rather than the [[substance]] of a [[text]].
#: {{ant|en|substantive}}
# Consisting of words only.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1864|author=w:Henry Mayhew|title=German Life and Manners as Seen in Saxony at the Present
|passage=We subjoin an engraving {{...}} which will give the reader a far better notion of the structure than any '''verbal''' description could convey to the mind.}}
